Ladybird defines engine-specific interfaces and members only while the
navigator claims that engine. Blink implements navigator.deviceMemory
in NavigatorDeviceMemory and exposes WebGLObject through its WebIDL;
neither WebKit nor Gecko has either. Gecko’s Navigator::GetBuildID()
returns the fixed “20181001000000” (LEGACY_BUILD_ID in nsContentUtils)
for web content, its Navigator::GetOscpu() the platform token
(nsHttpHandler’s mOscpu, “Intel Mac OS X 10.15” on macOS), and
Navigator::TaintEnabled() false; Blink and WebKit have none of the
three. Ladybird derives oscpu from the User-Agent string’s platform
tokens so a spoofed Firefox User-Agent and oscpu agree.
